ocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\ngodot 4.3.stable official binary\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.19045 - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6590) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700KF (24 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\ncallback function set by DisplayServer.tts_set_utterance_callback will be called in a weird order once DisplayServer.tts_stop() was called to interrupt a speech; \r\ne.g. if speechA is playing and i want to play speechB, then i call tts_stop() and then tts_speak(speechB, voice), the callback function will be in this order:\r\n1. callback_for_utterance_cancel of speechA\r\n2. callback_for_utterance_boundary of speechB (sometimes, but no more than one time, and the character_id is incorrect)\r\n3. callback_fot_utterance_end of speechB (almost always)\r\n4. and there's no others, until speechB finishes\r\n\r\nit may have something about the queue, but i really want the _interrupting speech_ (speechB in the example above) can have callback functions called from utterance_start, and have other callbacks work normally\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\ncan be found in the MRP below\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[tts_issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17729180/tts_issue.zip)\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"